{
  "_comment": [
    "SYNTHETIC — hand-built from the documented response shapes in Yahoo's official",
    "Fantasy Sports API guide and from published wrapper-library samples (yfpy,",
    "yahoo_fantasy_api). NOT a live capture. Yahoo API access is gated behind an",
    "approval application and NO live call has ever been made from this repo.",
    "Replace with a real redacted capture once API access is approved.",
    "",
    "AUTHORED 2026-08-11 (not captured on any date).",
    "MODELS: GET /fantasy/v2/users;use_login=1/games/leagues",
    "            ?game_keys=423,449,461,465&format=json",
    "",
    "REDACTION: the authenticating user's guid is FAKEGUID00000000000004 and",
    "every league/team id below is invented. A real capture of THIS endpoint",
    "returns the login's own guid and may return an email on the user resource —",
    "both must be stripped before anything from it is committed. The parser",
    "deliberately never reads email even when Yahoo sends it.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS IS COMMITTED — CROSS-SEASON DISCOVERY IS THE WHOLE POINT OF THE",
    "PIPELINE, and it has two independent failure modes, both encoded here.",
    "",
    "  A. THE GAME-ID PROBLEM. Season → game_key is NOT derivable: 2023=423,",
    "     2024=449, 2025=461, and (from other seasons) 2019=390, 2020=399. There",
    "     is no pattern. A hardcoded game id does not error — it silently queries",
    "     a DIFFERENT SEASON and returns perfectly valid rows for the wrong year.",
    "     Game keys must be enumerated from the provider and persisted, which is",
    "     what this response is for.",
    "",
    "  B. THE FILTER. Game 465 below is NHL. It has a league, that league parses",
    "     cleanly, and it has absolutely nothing to do with football. Discovery",
    "     MUST filter by game_code before it walks anything — note that",
    "     parse_user_leagues() itself does NOT filter (it faithfully returns all",
    "     four leagues, NHL included); the filtering is YahooProvider.",
    "     discover_leagues()'s job. The assertion worth writing is that the parser",
    "     returns 4 and the provider returns 3.",
    "",
    "     ⚠️ A RELATED TRAP NOT REPRODUCED HERE, because reproducing it would mean",
    "     inventing a shape rather than recording one: Yahoo's own docs warn that",
    "     requesting /users;use_login=1/games/leagues UNFILTERED throws outright",
    "     if the account ever played a game type with no league sub-resource",
    "     (pick'em, DFS). That is why the adapter enumerates games FIRST, filters",
    "     to code=nfl and type=full client-side, and only then asks for leagues by",
    "     explicit game key. This fixture models the already-filtered request.",
    "",
    "THE RENEWAL CHAIN, which is the second discovery mechanism:",
    "    423.l.481226 (2023)  renew ''            renewed '449_529351'",
    "    449.l.529351 (2024)  renew '423_481226'  renewed '461_576919'",
    "    461.l.576919 (2025)  renew '449_529351'  renewed ''",
    "Note the FORMAT: renew/renewed use an UNDERSCORE ('449_529351'), which is",
    "NOT a league key. canonical_league_key() rewrites it to '449.l.529351';",
    "storing both forms would produce phantom duplicates of one league. Note also",
    "that the league_id CHANGES every season — each season is a separate league",
    "object and only the chain connects them.",
    "",
    "WHY BOTH MECHANISMS EXIST: this account-based query only reaches seasons the",
    "AUTHENTICATING account actually played. If the league changed hands, or the",
    "account joined in 2024, the 2023 season is invisible here — but the chain",
    "still points at it. Neither mechanism alone is complete; the union is. The",
    "2023 entry is present here so the two can be tested as agreeing, and its",
    "empty renew is what tells the walker to stop rather than loop.",
    "",
    "SHAPE HAZARDS DELIBERATELY PRESENT:",
    "  1. The deepest nesting in the whole API: users → user → games → game →",
    "     leagues → league, alternating COLLECTION (numeric keys + count) and",
    "     RESOURCE (heterogeneous array) at every level, with the user's own",
    "     metadata nested one array deeper than that.",
    "  2. renew is \"\" on the oldest season — Yahoo's self-closing element, meaning",
    "     'not renewed from anything'. canonical_league_key('') returns None,",
    "     which is the correct storage: no previous season exists. That is a",
    "     different fact from the key being absent.",
    "  3. season arrives as a STRING on the games and league_id as a string",
    "     everywhere, while num_teams is a bare int.",
    "  4. The NHL league has num_teams 10 and a scoring_type of 'head' too — it",
    "     is not distinguishable by anything except game_code. Do not try.",
    "",
    "NOT TRUNCATED: 4 games, one league each, is the complete response for this",
    "invented account."
  ],
